hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"223","On marrying equals: Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Ibn Hurmuz al-Fadaki narrated to us, from Sa'id and Muhammad, the two sons of Ubayd, from Abu Hatim al-Muzani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one comes to you whose religion and character you approve of, marry him to her - three times."
"224","Qutaybah [ibn Sa'id] narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Abdullah ibn Hurmuz al-Yamani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the same; he said: The people pressed him, so he repeated it three times. Abu Dawud said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman has transmitted it with a connected chain from Ibn Ajlan, and it is a mistake."
"225","Abdullah ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Bilal to a household of the Ansar to propose to them, and they said: A black Abyssinian slave! So Bilal said: Had the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not commanded me to come to you, I would not have come to you. They said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded you? He said: Yes. They said: You have taken possession. So he came [to] the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him, and a piece of gold was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave it to him and said: Drive this to your wife; and he said to his Companions: Gather for your brother for his wedding feast."
"226","Uthman narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Amir, who said: Bilal went with his brother to propose on his behalf to some people of the Arabs, and they said: Two Abyssinian slaves! [So Bilal said: Yes,] we were astray and Allah guided us, and we were slaves and Allah - [the Mighty and Majestic] - freed us."
"227","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah; he mentioned it, from Muharib, who said: If you marry us, praise be to Allah; and if you turn us away, Allah is Greatest."
"228","Harun ibn Zayd narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Zayd ibn Aslam, that Banu Bukayr came to [the Messenger of Allah] (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Marry our sister to so-and-so. He said: Why not Bilal? They repeated, and he repeated the words three times, so they married her to him. He said: Banu Bukayr were among the Emigrants of Banu Layth."
"229","Amr ibn Uthman and Kathir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, both said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, al-Zubaydi narrated to me; al-Zuhri narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Banu Bayadah to marry Abu Hind to a woman of theirs, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we marry our daughters to our freedmen? So Allah - [the Mighty and Majestic] - revealed: (Indeed We created you from male and female and made you peoples and tribes) - the verse. al-Zuhri said: It was revealed specifically concerning Abu Hind. Abu Dawud said: Part of it has been narrated with a connected chain, and it is weak."
"230","Isa ibn Yunus al-Tarsusi narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Amr ibn Dinar: that Bilal had under him a Qurayshi woman."
"231","Ibn Ubayd narrated to us, in the hadith of Hammad from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, that a man married his daughter while she was unwilling, so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: Do you dislike him? She said: Yes, so he put her affair in her own hand."
